WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.143
"Why Don't Health Insurers
Encourage Healthier Eating?"

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:14.160
Many of the diseases that
cause a constant drain

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:18.160
on health care budgets can be
prevented by proper nutrition.

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:21.520
So why aren't the big
payors getting involved?

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:25.181
I mean, even like a 1% decline
in excess body fat could

00:00:25.181 --> 00:00:28.400
alone save tens of billions.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:31.600
You'd think at least the health
insurance industry would try

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:34.960
to get people to eat healthier
to try to pay out less money.

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:40.240
Well, one could say the insurance
industry actually benefits from

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:43.520
high health care costs because
these rising costs are simply

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:46.240
passed on to both individuals
and employers in terms of

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:50.000
higher premiums, and
insurers take a fixed percentage

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:53.040
of these premiums
as increasing profits.

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:56.640
They get a piece of the pie,
so the bigger the pie —

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:00.880
the unhealthier everyone is —
the bigger their piece.

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:04.560
As such, insurers have not
done as much as they could

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:07.440
to help reduce health care
costs because lower costs

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:10.776
would hurt their bottom line.

00:01:10.776 --> 00:01:14.000
What if there was a medication
that could successfully treat

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:17.280
and even reverse heart disease,
type 2 diabetes, high blood pressure,

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:21.360
and many other chronic conditions
without any negative side effects and

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:25.200
offered the promise of dramatically
reduced health care costs?

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:28.160
Imagine all the advertising
there would be to promote it.

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:30.160
Imagine how much
they would charge.

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:32.880
A drug that could not just
treat but cure diabetes

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:35.040
and these other diseases?

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:38.320
Then what if you were told
that medication exists today,

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:42.560
is available to everyone in
unlimited quantities at a low cost,

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:46.560
but the vast majority of the American
public has never heard about it.

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:50.720
You want a solution to significantly
reduce health care costs?

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:55.040
The solution is to use food
as medical treatment,

00:01:55.040 --> 00:02:00.362
specifically foods made from
minimally processed plants.

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:03.840
One of the main barriers is simply
the current widespread belief

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:06.080
that once someone has
a chronic condition,

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:08.400
such as heart disease,
type 2 diabetes,

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:11.600
there's very little that can be done
to actually reverse the disease,

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:15.360
and the best outcome possible
is to maintain the condition

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:18.240
so that it just
doesn't get any worse.

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:20.480
The fact that a whole food
plant-based approach provides

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:24.320
a safe, effective, low-cost alternative
to not just eliminating symptoms

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:27.520
but potentially reversing
the underlying condition

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:29.200
without drugs or surgery

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:32.160
is unknown to a vast
majority of Americans.

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:35.840
In contrast to the pharmaceutical
industry that spends large sums

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:39.360
to market new drugs, there are
not big profits in promoting

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:41.840
a plant-based diet.

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:46.080
The politics surrounding healthcare
is who's going to pay for it,

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:49.600
instead of what kind
of healthcare is best?

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:52.880
And the evidence is overwhelming
that a whole food, plant-based diet

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:56.560
provides the best opportunity to not
only reduce the growth in spending,

00:02:56.560 --> 00:03:00.480
but actually decrease total health
care costs more than any drug,

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:05.760
medical procedure, insurance reform,
or provider payment model out there.

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:08.800
Thankfully, the word is spreading.

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:12.000
A review of the evidence published
in Kaiser Permanente's journal

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:14.400
concluded that physicians should
consider recommending

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:17.840
a plant-based diet to all their
patients, especially those

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:22.000
with high blood pressure, diabetes,
cardiovascular disease, or obesity.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:25.120
Kaiser has followed up
with user friendly guides

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:26.400
(freely available online)

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:29.120
for both physicians and patients,
explaining the benefits

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:33.040
and practical aspects of
implementing a plant-based diet.

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:37.040
So hey, why aren't all insurers
sending out such information

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:39.040
to all their members?

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:41.840
You know how all the
drug ads are like,

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:44.400
"Ask your doctor if this
drug is right for you."

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:48.320
Well, members could be
prompted to ask their physicians

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:52.320
about the ability of plant-based
diets to reduce or eliminate

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:54.640
prescription drug use,
reverse disease.

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:57.680
Though, of course, these
materials would also have

00:03:57.680 --> 00:04:01.600
to list all the side effects.
Side effects include

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:04.480
increased energy, lower blood
pressure, improved digestion,

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:07.440
all while eating unlimited
quantities of satisfying food.

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:12.493
Ask your doctor if
plants are right for you.

